{"surface": "event", "title": "The FDA approves Novo Nordisk's CagriSema by March 31, 2027", "html": "<div class=\"ev ws\"><div class=\"evh\"><h2 class=\"title\">The FDA approves Novo Nordisk&#x27;s CagriSema by March 31, 2027</h2><p class=\"facts\"><span>Any time to Mar 31, 2027</span><span class=\"sep\">·</span><span class=\"src\">Known from FDA; Novo Nordisk company announcement</span></p><div class=\"hds\"><details class=\"hd\" data-k=\"definition\"><summary>Definition</summary><div class=\"hdb text\"><p>The US Food and Drug Administration approves CagriSema (cagrilintide 2.4 mg / semaglutide 2.4 mg) for chronic weight management on or before March 31, 2027. Novo filed in December 2025 and expects a decision in the fourth quarter of 2026. No covers a complete response letter, or no decision by that date.</p></div></details><details class=\"hd\" data-k=\"notes\"><summary>Rationale</summary><div class=\"hdb\"><div class=\"note\" data-k=\"note:62\" data-note=\"note:62\"><div class=\"md\" data-md=\"Kalshi asks approval before January 1 and before July 1, 2027. Novo &#x27;expects a decision in the fourth quarter of 2026&#x27;; if that slips past year-end without a rejection, the usual cause is a review extension of about three months, which lands by the end of March. I put 7 parts in 10 of a first-half approval by March 31 (2 by mid-February, 5 by end-March) and 3 later.\"><p>Kalshi asks approval before January 1 and before July 1, 2027. Novo &#x27;expects a decision in the fourth quarter of 2026&#x27;; if that slips past year-end without a rejection, the usual cause is a review extension of about three months, which lands by the end of March. I put 7 parts in 10 of a first-half approval by March 31 (2 by mid-February, 5 by end-March) and 3 later.</p></div></div><h4 class=\"ev-k\">Evidence</h4><div class=\"basis\"><p class=\"src\"><a class=\"go\" data-go=\"src:110\">benzinga.com</a></p><blockquote class=\"q\"><a class=\"go quote\" data-go=\"x:passage:src:110:a8567fd9e1bd\">Novo Nordisk filed a New Drug Application with the U.S. Food and Drug Administration in December 2025 for CagriSema 2.4 mg / 2.4 mg and expects a decision in the fourth quarter of 2026.</a></blockquote></div></div></details></div></div><div class=\"strip\" data-count=\"6\" style=\"--cols:5\"><div class=\"sf first\" data-k=\"fig:Forecast\"><span class=\"lab\">Forecast</span><span class=\"v\"><a class=\"go num\" data-go=\"x:p:prop:6\"><span class=\"n v\">92.0%</span></a></span><a class=\"cap go calc\" data-go=\"x:p:prop:6\">How it’s set →</a></div><div class=\"sf\" data-k=\"fig:Market range\"><span class=\"lab\">Market range</span><span class=\"v\"><a class=\"go num\" data-go=\"x:interval:prop:6\"><span class=\"n v\">92.0%</span></a></span></div><div class=\"sf\" data-k=\"fig:If Yes\"><span class=\"lab\">If Yes</span><span class=\"v\"><a class=\"go num\" data-go=\"x:outcome:prop:6:yes\"><span class=\"n v gain\">+$107</span></a></span><span class=\"cap\"><span class=\"n gain\">+0.02%</span> of portfolio</span></div><div class=\"sf\" data-k=\"fig:If No\"><span class=\"lab\">If No</span><span class=\"v\"><a class=\"go num\" data-go=\"x:outcome:prop:6:no\"><span class=\"n v loss\">−$1,228</span></a></span></div><div class=\"sf\" data-k=\"fig:Full impact\"><span class=\"lab\">Full impact</span><span class=\"v\"><a class=\"go num\" data-go=\"x:swing:prop:6\"><span class=\"n v gain\">+$1,335</span></a></span></div><div class=\"sf\" data-k=\"fig:Volatility\"><span class=\"lab\">Volatility</span><span class=\"v\"><a class=\"go num\" data-go=\"x:volatility:prop:6\"><span class=\"n v\">±$362</span></a></span></div></div><nav class=\"tabs\" role=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" role=\"tab\" data-tab=\"outcomes\">Outcomes</button><button type=\"button\" role=\"tab\" data-tab=\"probability\">Probability</button><button type=\"button\" role=\"tab\" data-tab=\"assumptions\">Assumptions</button></nav><section data-pane=\"outcomes\"><div class=\"ev-card po-card\" data-k=\"pay